    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds incredibly exhausting to feel trapped in that same cycle of failure and shame, but please know that your persistence in trying to get things right is still a sign of strength, even when it doesn't feel like it right now. Gaining control over an obsessive pattern isn't about stopping the old thoughts immediately, but learning that progress is often made by noticing the loop, feeling the weight of it without letting it define you, and taking just one small step forward before you spiral again. You are not broken for struggling; you are human, and sometimes the goal isn't never falling apart again but building a kindness toward yourself so you can get through the next inevitable stumble without crushing your spirit.",
