    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear you, but it feels like i'm just lying to myself when i try to be \"kind\" to myself. like, how am i supposed to feel better about the fact that i'm just a person who can't even stay sober for a few months? it feels like a waste of time. just a constant cycle of starting over and failing. i just wonder if there's even a point to the struggle anymore.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear that deep sense of futility when feeling like your efforts are completely wasted, but remember that struggling isn't about feeling better immediately or achieving perfect sobriety overnight; often, simply showing up to fight the next round against the loop is enough to keep the momentum alive. You don't need to love yourself *through* the shame or the failure to progress; sometimes acknowledging the pain and refusing to stop trying, however imperfectly, is far more powerful than hiding behind a forced \"okay everything.\" Think of it not as a straight line to a destination that feels out of reach, but as a messy, winding path where every stumble actually teaches you something about your resilience that you couldn't learn otherwise.",
